Description: Wild OS Settings
 The Settings app of Wild OS, laid out and worded the way Windows 11
 Settings is: system, devices, network, personalisation, apps, Windows apps,
 accounts, time and language, privacy and security, and updates. Wild OS's
 own pages drive the system through the same services the desktop uses;
 KDE's settings modules are shown inside it where Wild OS has no page of its
 own yet.
 .
 Its keyboard, printer, account, language and app permission pages work
 through kxkbrc and KWin, CUPS, AccountsService and two small root helpers,
 the regional settings KDE uses and Flatpak's override files.
 .
 It also points the desktop's right-click "Personalise" entry at Settings
 and installs the small helper that sets automatic security updates.
